  "title": "Erdős Problem #939",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $r\\geq 2$. An $r$-powerful number $n$ is one such that if $p\\mid n$ then $p^r\\mid n$.\nIf $r\\geq 4$ then can the sum of $r-2$ coprime $r$-powerful numbers ever be itself $r$-powerful? Are there at most finitely many such solutions?\nAre there infinitely many triples of coprime $3$-powerful numbers $a,b,c$ such that $a+b=c$?",
